    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- E₄.resToImagAxis s (real part) → 1 as s → ∞. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E₄_re_resToImagAxis_tendsto_one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Tendsto</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E₄</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">resToImagAxis</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">re</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">atTop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nhds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E₄_resToImagAxis_tendsto_one</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">tendsto_cont</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- H₂.resToImagAxis s (real part) tends to 0 as s → ∞. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H₂_re_resToImagAxis_tendsto_zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Tendsto</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">H₂</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">resToImagAxis</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">re</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">atTop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nhds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H₂_resToImagAxis_tendsto_zero</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">tendsto_cont</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- H₄.resToImagAxis s (real part) tends to 1 as s → ∞. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H₄_re_resToImagAxis_tendsto_one</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Tendsto</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">H₄</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">resToImagAxis</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">re</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">atTop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nhds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H₄_resToImagAxis_tendsto_one</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">tendsto_cont</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- The numerator expression N(s) = s² * FReal s - 12/π * s * (F₁*E₄)(is) + 36/π² * E₄(is)²</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  tends to 36/π² as s → ∞. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">numerator_tendsto_at_infty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Tendsto</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">12</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">F₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E₄</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">resToImagAxis</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">re</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">36</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E₄</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toFun</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">resToImagAxis</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">re</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">atTop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nhds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">36</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sq_mul_FReal_tendsto_zero</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul_F₁E₄_re_tendsto_zero</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E₄_re_resToImagAxis_tendsto_one</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">tendsto_cont</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 580095652,
        "sender_full_name": "Cameron Freer",
        "timestamp": 1773806123
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That looks great for me! Could you briefly explain what actually happened in <a href=\"https://github.com/thefundamentaltheor3m/Sphere-Packing-Lean/pull/367\">spherepacking#367</a>?</p>",
        "id": 580096056,
        "sender_full_name": "Seewoo Lee",
        "timestamp": 1773806257
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In the course of reviewing <a href=\"https://github.com/thefundamentaltheor3m/Sphere-Packing-Lean/pull/330\">spherepacking#330</a>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"246273\">@Bhavik Mehta</span> <a href=\"https://github.com/thefundamentaltheor3m/Sphere-Packing-Lean/pull/330#discussion_r2908511083\">noticed that <code>whnfR</code> wasn't needed</a> for any of the examples, and so we removed it.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/thefundamentaltheor3m/Sphere-Packing-Lean/pull/367\">spherepacking#367</a> restores this (and uses <code>whnf</code> rather than <code>whnfR</code> to unfold regular <code>def</code>s as well as <code>@[reducible]</code> definitions (like <code>abbrev</code>).  As I understand it, there are two things going on:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><code>whnfR</code> performs beta-reduction at the head of the expression, after which <code>matchTendsto?</code> or <code>matchNhds?</code> can see the <code>Filter.Tendsto ...</code> or <code>nhds ...</code> inside it.</li>\n<li><code>whnf</code> unfolds definitions to their lambda bodies in cases where the goal function is a named definition rather than a literal lambda. (e.g., in your <code>denominator_tendsto_at_infty</code>, the <code>change</code> is no longer needed to expose the lambda.)</li>\n</ol>",
        "id": 580192710,
        "sender_full_name": "Cameron Freer",
        "timestamp": 1773840815
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>update: in response to <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"246273\">@Bhavik Mehta</span> 's feedback, now <a href=\"https://github.com/thefundamentaltheor3m/Sphere-Packing-Lean/pull/367\">spherepacking#367</a> uses <code>whnfR</code> rather than <code>whnf</code> throughout -- I think this may now require a <code>change</code> or <code>show</code> when working with <code>def</code> rather than <code>abbrev</code>, but it sounds like this is appropriate and matches the way tactics like <code>fun_prop</code> and <code>continuity</code> behave.</p>",
        "id": 580263420,
        "sender_full_name": "Cameron Freer",
        "timestamp": 1773857898
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is the <code>whnf</code> needed for Seewoo's example? I'd hope not...</p>",
        "id": 580263871,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1773858042
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Seewoo's example still works, as do the first 3 I added, but <code>numerator_tendsto_at_infty</code> now fails (it involves <code>zpow</code> and non-reducible <code>FReal</code>/<code>resToImagAxis</code> in the atoms).</p>",
        "id": 580264893,
        "sender_full_name": "Cameron Freer",
        "timestamp": 1773858391
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh hold on, why is <code>zpow</code> an issue? I think it's acceptable if the user has to unfold semireducible defs in order for the tactic to fire, matching fun_prop/continuity/linarith/simp</p>",
        "id": 580298444,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1773871556
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"246273\">@Bhavik Mehta</span> I approved <a href=\"https://github.com/thefundamentaltheor3m/Sphere-Packing-Lean/pull/378\">PR#378</a> since it works for myself - do you have further comments on it? Otherwise we can probably merge it.</p>",
        "id": 585459083,
        "sender_full_name": "Seewoo Lee",
        "timestamp": 1776180685
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"246273\">@Bhavik Mehta</span> now <a href=\"https://github.com/thefundamentaltheor3m/Sphere-Packing-Lean/pull/378\">spherepacking#378</a> is merged, but do you have any comments on <a href=\"https://github.com/thefundamentaltheor3m/Sphere-Packing-Lean/pull/384\">spherepacking#384</a>? In the last packathon, it sounded like we wanted to potentially merge it before coordinating on <code>fun_prop</code> extensions as in <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/computing.20derivatives.20with.20fun_prop/near/582571823\">#mathlib4 &gt; computing derivatives with fun_prop @ 💬</a> .</p>",
        "id": 604744843,
        "sender_full_name": "Cameron Freer",
        "timestamp": 1781841651
    }
